-- MeshSwap: swaps the part-built rocks (crags, rock clusters, ledges, sea stacks, arches, reef
-- shelves/pinnacles) for the deformed, stud-textured Blender meshes. The part terrain (stacked
-- slab cliffs, ground, paths, shallows) stays as parts, so the meshes sit in and blend with it,
-- like the coral reef.
--
-- 1. File > Import 3D > exports/meshes/VoxelRockMeshes.fbx   (all rocks, it lands in Workspace)
-- 2. Paste this whole file into the Command Bar (View > Command Bar) and press Enter.
--
-- Optional: TERRAIN_MESH = true also covers each island's cliffs with one deformed terrain mesh
-- (import exports/meshes/<IslandName>_Terrain.fbx first). The ground then becomes invisible collision.
--
-- Every mesh piece is placed from its exact size/centre (baked in below by Blender),
-- so it doesn't matter how the importer scaled or grouped the meshes.
-- Running it again is safe. Set UNDO = true and run it to put the part rocks back.

local UNDO = false
local TERRAIN_MESH = false

